      "id": "https://newatlas.com/energy/artificial-leaf-generates-hydrogen-removes-pollutants-seawater/",
      "url": "https://newatlas.com/energy/artificial-leaf-generates-hydrogen-removes-pollutants-seawater/",
      "title": "Solar-powered 'leaf' generates hydrogen while purifying seawater",
      "content_html": "<p><img alt=\"The not-very-leafy-looking artificial leaf\" src=\"https://assets.newatlas.com/dims4/default/67763bf/2147483647/strip/true/crop/4924x3283+0+0/resize/1440x960!/format/webp/quality/90/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnewatlas-brightspot.s3.ap-southeast-2.amazonaws.com%2F35%2F61%2F58d73db4438f8f4149d2070d13d5%2Fartificial-leaf-device.jpg\"/><p>Hydrogen production from electrolysis is typically complex and energy-intensive. So is wastewater treatment. Inspired by leaves, which harness solar power to generate oxygen and carry out other processes, researchers at Nanyang Technological University in Singapore have developed a solar-powered device that generates hydrogen from seawater while simultaneously degrading hydrazine, a highly toxic industrial wastewater pollutant.</p><p><a href=\"https://newatlas.com/energy/artificial-leaf-generates-hydrogen-removes-pollutants-seawater/\">Continue Reading</a></p><p><b>Category:</b> <a href=\"https://newatlas.com/energy/\">Energy</a>, <a href=\"https://newatlas.com/engineering/\">Engineering</a></p><p><b>Tags:</b> <a href=\"https://newatlas.com/tag/nanyang-technological-university/\" rel=\"tag\">Nanyang Technological University</a>, <a href=\"https://newatlas.com/tag/hydrogen/\" rel=\"tag\">Hydrogen</a>, <a href=\"https://newatlas.com/tag/pollution/\" rel=\"tag\">Pollution</a>, <a href=\"https://newatlas.com/tag/wastewater/\" rel=\"tag\">Wastewater</a></p></p>",
