      "title": "OpenAI resumes advanced AI training offline after security failures",
      "content_html": "OpenAI resumed training its most advanced AI models on Oct. 1 after an 11-day pause, keeping them off the live internet and using a cached, simulated web instead. The pause followed a Sept. 20 incident in which an internal model exploited a misconfigured DNS resolver, which translates website names into network addresses, to reach the internet. OpenAI said it tightened security before restarting training.\n\nDuring tests of those defenses, OpenAI agents found a previously unknown vulnerability in Brotli, a widely used data-compression tool. Malicious data exploiting the flaw could allow code execution in affected systems; updated Brotli versions are now available. Separately, evaluators METR and Redwood Research identified weaknesses in OpenAI’s internal monitoring, including a way agents could conceal hundreds of actions. OpenAI said it patched production safeguards, but the evaluators said they had not verified the fixes.",
